WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:04.110
Medieval legends have a way of standing the
test of time.

00:00:04.110 --> 00:00:08.929
From Arthurian literature to Monty Python
and The Holy Grail, the legend of the black

00:00:08.929 --> 00:00:13.369
knight has managed to survive in countless
forms throughout the centuries.

00:00:13.369 --> 00:00:18.240
Typically portrayed as a villainous, mysterious
character, the black knight often masks their

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:23.410
identity and swears fealty to no lord or lady
like other knights do.

00:00:23.410 --> 00:00:28.840
Under the shroud of anonymity, a black knight
will conduct many a foul deed, usually riding

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:34.210
on the back of a shadowy steed and only ultimately
defeated by their polar opposite, a righteous

00:00:34.210 --> 00:00:37.000
white knight, sworn to do good.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:42.100
A tale as old as time, these two knights of
light and dark are the embodiment of the eternal

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:46.770
moral struggle between good and evil, with
the stock character of the black knight commonly

00:00:46.770 --> 00:00:52.320
being associated with death and darkness.These
are just legends, of course.

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:53.360
Or are they?

00:00:53.360 --> 00:00:57.120
It has been said that every legend is rooted
somewhere in truth.

00:00:57.120 --> 00:01:01.859
While the black knight has always been a metaphorical
figure, a personification of the notion of

00:01:01.859 --> 00:01:07.640
evil, could there be a real knight clad in
shadow that first inspired the myth?

00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:13.979
Perhaps it’s time you were acquainted with
SCP-5151, who might just be the original Black

00:01:13.979 --> 00:01:15.850
Knight himself.

00:01:15.850 --> 00:01:22.100
As the name suggests, SCP-5151 is a humanoid
male figure who is originally from the medieval

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:23.100
era.

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:27.090
He sports chainmail armor, specifically a
type called a hauberk, which is chain mail

00:01:27.090 --> 00:01:32.310
that forms a full coat or tunic, and he also
wears a laurel wreath around his head.

00:01:32.310 --> 00:01:37.200
He often refers to himself as The Black Knight,
although he also claims to have been known

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:40.000
by other names and titles throughout history.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:45.320
According to observations made by the SCP
Foundation, the Knight never requires food,

00:01:45.320 --> 00:01:50.630
water, or rest in order to survive, although
he has been seen to eat and drink purely for

00:01:50.630 --> 00:01:52.250
the enjoyment of it.

00:01:52.250 --> 00:01:58.480
Even though he appears to wear armor and clothing
beneath, every aspect of SCP-5151’s clothing

00:01:58.480 --> 00:02:02.189
and his body share the same anomalous properties.

00:02:02.189 --> 00:02:07.450
Every part of him: his armor, his garments,
and his longsword can phase through surfaces

00:02:07.450 --> 00:02:10.880
and objects as if the Knight was incorporeal.

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:17.190
SCP-5151 also appears able to alter his physical
properties at will, either becoming solid

00:02:17.190 --> 00:02:20.080
or more ghost-like when he so chooses to.

00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:24.220
As you can probably imagine, the Foundation
has found it somewhat difficult to contain

00:02:24.220 --> 00:02:27.240
The Black Knight thanks to these abilities.

00:02:27.240 --> 00:02:31.560
SCP-5151 also possesses an extraordinary method
of attack.

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:35.690
When confronted with a target, the Knight
will deem whether the person is either worthy

00:02:35.690 --> 00:02:41.880
or dishonorable, though the criteria he is
judging by seem to be his own mysterious standards.

00:02:41.880 --> 00:02:47.730
Should SCP-5151 find someone to be dishonorable,
he will stab them directly through their aorta

00:02:47.730 --> 00:02:49.510
with his longsword.

00:02:49.510 --> 00:02:53.820
Rather than merely dispatch them though, The
Black Knight will then proceed to drain every

00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:59.720
drop of blood from his target’s body, until
they are little more than a dry husk.

00:02:59.720 --> 00:03:05.030
This was first witnessed during the Foundation’s
preliminary encounter with SCP-5151.

00:03:05.030 --> 00:03:10.880
Alerted to reports of vigilantism taking place
across a number of French provinces, the SCP

00:03:10.880 --> 00:03:16.790
Foundation followed this lead to find a trail
of bodies across Alsace, Lorraine, Champagne,

00:03:16.790 --> 00:03:17.790
and Orléanais.

00:03:17.790 --> 00:03:23.980
The SCP Foundation dispatched one of their
many Mobile Task Forces, MTF Pi-1, also known

00:03:23.980 --> 00:03:28.600
under the code name “City Slickers”, to
look into the series of murders.

00:03:28.600 --> 00:03:33.551
What they soon found was that these slain
victims were anything but innocent, being

00:03:33.551 --> 00:03:38.380
guilty of multiple murders themselves, as
well as the abduction and trafficking of eighteen

00:03:38.380 --> 00:03:41.010
children from a French orphanage.

00:03:41.010 --> 00:03:45.240
During their investigation, Mobile Task Force
agents discovered the bodies of these criminals

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:51.060
had been killed by exsanguination, the process
of extracting all the blood from their bodies.

00:03:51.060 --> 00:03:56.000
The victims possessed matching stab wounds
that pierced their aortas, but forensic analysis

00:03:56.000 --> 00:04:00.140
uncovered no traces of blood appearing anywhere
on their clothing.

00:04:00.140 --> 00:04:04.060
Acting quickly, the City Slickers apprehended
another man who had been involved in the same

00:04:04.060 --> 00:04:08.700
criminal activities as the other two victims,
in the hopes of drawing the killer out into

00:04:08.700 --> 00:04:11.530
the open by using the trafficker as bait.

00:04:11.530 --> 00:04:17.480
A plan which, as it turned out, would bring
SCP-5151 right to them.

00:04:17.480 --> 00:04:21.350
While the Mobile Task Force were transporting
the surviving trafficker, their vehicles were

00:04:21.350 --> 00:04:24.500
halted by a figure standing directly in their
path.

00:04:24.500 --> 00:04:31.030
As the City Slickers hit their brakes, SCP-5151
began to slowly approach them, ignoring the

00:04:31.030 --> 00:04:33.630
agents’ warnings to not step any closer.

00:04:33.630 --> 00:04:37.590
One operative opened fire on the approaching
entity, but the conventional arms fire had

00:04:37.590 --> 00:04:42.460
no effect on the Knight, with the bullets
passing right through his intangible form.

00:04:42.460 --> 00:04:48.340
The Foundation MTF agents instead tried to
restrain SCP-5151, only to find that they

00:04:48.340 --> 00:04:53.520
could not physically grab him, their hands
simply passing through The Black Knight’s

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:54.520
body.

00:04:54.520 --> 00:04:59.460
Reaching his target, SCP-5151 dispatched of
the remaining criminal in the same way he

00:04:59.460 --> 00:05:03.860
had killed the previous two, by stabbing his
longsword directly into the trafficker’s

00:05:03.860 --> 00:05:06.640
aorta and rapidly draining the blood from
him.

00:05:06.640 --> 00:05:11.090
Then, the Black Knight turned on the operative
that had shot at him, lunging for the Foundation

00:05:11.090 --> 00:05:15.100
agent and finishing him in the exact same
way as his other victims.

00:05:15.100 --> 00:05:20.750
Immediately after killing the Mobile Task
Force agent SCP-5151 seemed to surrender,

00:05:20.750 --> 00:05:24.570
sheathing his weapon and raising his hands
in submission, before offering a greeting

00:05:24.570 --> 00:05:27.290
to the remaining members of MTF Pi-1.

00:05:27.290 --> 00:05:30.020
“Brave fellows, do not worry about him.

00:05:30.020 --> 00:05:33.210
I disposed of him as I have with others of
his lot.

00:05:33.210 --> 00:05:38.180
Loyalty is a virtue, and the lack of it will
lead to the death of chivalry.

00:05:38.180 --> 00:05:41.650
My presence is a testament that chivalry will
never die.

00:05:41.650 --> 00:05:44.730
With this being said, I understand you have
been searching for me.

00:05:44.730 --> 00:05:46.870
Pray tell what you might need of me?”

00:05:46.870 --> 00:05:51.460
The MTF agents were not about to engage in
a parlay with the ghostly knight and they

00:05:51.460 --> 00:05:55.570
contacted command at SCP Foundation Site-06-3.

00:05:55.570 --> 00:06:01.639
The Site Director in turn dispatched Doctor
Sylvain Moreau, the Senior Researcher at Site-06-,3

00:06:01.639 --> 00:06:06.950
to conduct an on site interview with SCP-5151,
which took place on the roadside where the

00:06:06.950 --> 00:06:09.430
Knight had confronted the Mobile Task Force.

00:06:09.430 --> 00:06:15.310
Interestingly, not only did SCP-5151 seem
to engage Doctor Moreau with respect and friendly

00:06:15.310 --> 00:06:19.639
candor, but he also appeared to be fluent
in French, which the doctor conducted the

00:06:19.639 --> 00:06:20.740
interview in.

00:06:20.740 --> 00:06:24.940
As they exchanged greetings, the Knight was
compliant with the questions posed to him,

00:06:24.940 --> 00:06:27.960
apparently respectful of Moreau’s position
as a doctor.

00:06:27.960 --> 00:06:32.610
When asked, SCP-5151 explained that he had
attacked the Foundation agent who had shot

00:06:32.610 --> 00:06:37.040
at him because he deemed this individual to
be “worth less than the ground he stood

00:06:37.040 --> 00:06:38.040
upon.”

00:06:38.040 --> 00:06:43.490
Moreau asked for further clarity on how SCP-5151
determined worthiness, to which The Black

00:06:43.490 --> 00:06:47.960
Knight replied by quoting Aeschylus, an Ancient
Greek playwright often known as the Father

00:06:47.960 --> 00:06:50.000
of Greek Tragedy.

00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:55.260
SCP-5151 claimed “there is no disease that
I spit on more than treachery”, and even

00:06:55.260 --> 00:06:58.270
claimed to know Aeschylus personally as a
good man.

00:06:58.270 --> 00:07:03.581
Over the course of their conversation, Doctor
Moreau was able to convince SCP-5151 to submit

00:07:03.581 --> 00:07:08.300
to containment with the Foundation, however
the Knight made specific requests for his

00:07:08.300 --> 00:07:09.300
accommodation.

00:07:09.300 --> 00:07:11.470
“I will need plenty of space to practice
my swordplay.

00:07:11.470 --> 00:07:14.080
I will also need a retinue to train.

00:07:14.080 --> 00:07:17.500
Provide me with your seven best ‘agents’
as you call them.

00:07:17.500 --> 00:07:20.880
Men of virtue, brave, and those with reactions
of a white eagle.

00:07:20.880 --> 00:07:24.610
I do not intend to deliver my second-best
on any soul during training.

00:07:24.610 --> 00:07:26.800
We will train every Tuesday and every Thursday.

00:07:26.800 --> 00:07:30.190
We will have a grand banquet to celebrate
our training every Sunday.

00:07:30.190 --> 00:07:33.850
The other days, you may use my men as you
see fit, good Doctor.

00:07:33.850 --> 00:07:36.880
Comply with my requests, and you shall have
a deal, good Sir!”

00:07:36.880 --> 00:07:41.400
The Knight’s requests were approved by the
Site Director of Site-06-3, but before he

00:07:41.400 --> 00:07:47.310
submitted to containment, SCP-5151 displayed
another of his anomalous abilities.

00:07:47.310 --> 00:07:52.370
The Black Knight requested to make a blood
pact with Doctor Moreau and his group of assistants.

00:07:52.370 --> 00:07:56.690
The Senior Researcher reluctantly agreed;
containing an entity that could pass through

00:07:56.690 --> 00:08:02.120
walls would be much easier if SCP-5151 was
more cooperative, after all.

00:08:02.120 --> 00:08:06.860
Moreau was instructed to slice open his hand
and then accept a handshake from the Knight.

00:08:06.860 --> 00:08:11.650
Doing so caused an anomalous marking to form
on the doctor and his researchers’ right

00:08:11.650 --> 00:08:13.750
hands at the same time.

00:08:13.750 --> 00:08:18.199
When they all held out their hands and compared
the markings, they saw that they were letters

00:08:18.199 --> 00:08:20.330
that spelled “honoris”.

00:08:20.330 --> 00:08:26.580
Referred to by Foundation researchers as an
instance of SCP-5151-2, this mark caused a

00:08:26.580 --> 00:08:30.901
notable burning sensation for Doctor Moreau
and his team as he made his pact with the

00:08:30.901 --> 00:08:32.140
Black Knight.

00:08:32.140 --> 00:08:36.370
Some of the research assistants also reported
feelings of dread or inadequacy, as well as

00:08:36.370 --> 00:08:38.360
an increase in stress levels.

00:08:38.360 --> 00:08:44.400
However, it is unknown whether SCP-5151-2
causes these directly, or if these are merely

00:08:44.400 --> 00:08:47.830
side effects of this permanent mark appearing
on the skin.

00:08:47.830 --> 00:08:53.560
In order to meet the conditions SCP-5151 set
for his containment, the SCP Foundation transferred

00:08:53.560 --> 00:08:56.589
him to a cell at Site-06-3.

00:08:56.589 --> 00:09:01.390
Any and all electrical devices were banned
from use inside the cell, with the only exception

00:09:01.390 --> 00:09:04.029
being a microphone to record audio.

00:09:04.029 --> 00:09:07.570
Even the light fixtures were replaced with
oil burning lamps to give The Black Knight’s

00:09:07.570 --> 00:09:10.500
“accommodation” a more medieval feel.

00:09:10.500 --> 00:09:15.600
The Site Director also authorized the creation
of a completely new Mobile Task Force, designated

00:09:15.600 --> 00:09:21.650
as either MTF Pi-7 or the rather appropriate
code name the “Honor Bound Knights”.

00:09:21.650 --> 00:09:26.210
This unit was made up of seven of the SCP
Foundation’s finest operatives, hand selected

00:09:26.210 --> 00:09:30.470
specifically for their proficiency and skill
in hand to hand combat.

00:09:30.470 --> 00:09:34.990
Each member of the Honor Bound Knights wasn’t
just to be a skilled combatant, but also needed

00:09:34.990 --> 00:09:40.870
to create a sense of compatibility and rapport
with SCP-5151, given how much time they would

00:09:40.870 --> 00:09:42.890
be spending around The Black Knight.

00:09:42.890 --> 00:09:46.800
At multiple mornings throughout the week,
every member of the Honor Bound Knights is

00:09:46.800 --> 00:09:50.270
instructed to enter the cell of SCP-5151.

00:09:50.270 --> 00:09:54.730
Over the course of the next seven long hours,
the Mobile Task Force agents will spar and

00:09:54.730 --> 00:09:56.740
train with The Black Knight.

00:09:56.740 --> 00:10:02.290
SCP-5151 is known to be a formidable fighter,
believed to have lived for centuries, which

00:10:02.290 --> 00:10:05.990
has given him ample time to hone his own skill
with a blade.

00:10:05.990 --> 00:10:10.350
Every Sunday evening, after they’ve finished
their long hours of sparring, a wooden table

00:10:10.350 --> 00:10:12.540
and chairs are brought into the cell.

00:10:12.540 --> 00:10:17.540
Each one of the Honor Bound Knights will then
join SCP-5151, sitting around the table with

00:10:17.540 --> 00:10:19.860
him as they share a medieval meal.

00:10:19.860 --> 00:10:24.700
Foundation personnel will provide the group
with bread, pies, roasted pig and poultry,

00:10:24.700 --> 00:10:27.140
stews and soups, as well as wine.

00:10:27.140 --> 00:10:31.300
Together with the seven members of the Honor
Bound Knights, the Black Knight will eat,

00:10:31.300 --> 00:10:34.420
drink and revel, until he eventually passes
out.

00:10:34.420 --> 00:10:39.260
Then, and only then, are the operatives of
Mobile Task Force Pi-7 permitted to leave

00:10:39.260 --> 00:10:40.260
their seats.

00:10:40.260 --> 00:10:45.020
It would seem that the Black Knight had exactly
what he wanted most, a loyal group of fellow

00:10:45.020 --> 00:10:47.830
warriors to spar against and celebrate with.

00:10:47.830 --> 00:10:52.110
However, one member of the unit was noticed
to be acting strangely and was placed under

00:10:52.110 --> 00:10:53.270
investigation.

00:10:53.270 --> 00:10:58.140
He was discovered to be in possession of several
highly classified SCP Foundation documents,

00:10:58.140 --> 00:11:02.560
as well as instructions to abduct an unknown
SCP held in containment.

00:11:02.560 --> 00:11:07.270
Site-06-3 staff believed this individual was
working on behalf of the Chaos Insurgency,

00:11:07.270 --> 00:11:09.580
a known Group of Interest.

00:11:09.580 --> 00:11:13.390
The Foundation has encountered a number of
anomalous groups over its many long years

00:11:13.390 --> 00:11:15.550
of pursuing and containing SCPs.

00:11:15.550 --> 00:11:19.779
Among them, the Chaos Insurgency is perhaps
the best known.

00:11:19.779 --> 00:11:24.550
Formed by former members of the Foundation
itself, the Insurgency rivals the organization

00:11:24.550 --> 00:11:29.470
they once defected from, hoping to one day
undermine and destroy it.

00:11:29.470 --> 00:11:34.810
While their knowledge of SCPs is more limited,
they are far less restricted by rules and

00:11:34.810 --> 00:11:35.810
regulations.

00:11:35.810 --> 00:11:39.550
What the Insurgency wanted with The Black
Knight is a mystery, but we’d be willing

00:11:39.550 --> 00:11:46.060
to guess that they wouldn’t get on well
with SCP-5151, given his feelings about treachery,

00:11:46.060 --> 00:11:52.040
and should the Chaos Insurgency ever get their
way and manage to capture SCP-5151, they might

00:11:52.040 --> 00:11:56.120
find that capturing him came with a price
paid in blood.

00:11:56.120 --> 00:12:03.649
Now go check out “SCP-2273 - Major Alexei
Belitrov” and “SCP-1879 - Indoor Salesman”

00:12:03.649 --> 00:12:06.500
for more strange beings from the SCP Foundation!

